From bac5257a96fadcfd44929e385abd57cf0135dfff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:57:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/42] Network radio: use a QMX plugged into a Synology NAS
 over TCP/IP

Adds a "network radio" source so the Tab5 can use a QMX that is plugged
into a NAS instead of its own USB port.

Firmware:
- net/radio_relay.c/.h: QMXR/1 client (TCP 7355) carrying 48 kHz I/Q,
  CAT, and the QMX's second serial port for Radio menus.
- cat.c: every CAT write goes through cat_tx() (USB CDC or network);
  link_task picks the transport on each (re)connect; cat_reconnect(),
  cat_get_transport(); orderly shutdown returns a networked radio to RX.
- audio.c: audio_push_net_iq() feeds the same sample ring and RX audio
  path as the USB driver; a local USB QMX is ignored while the network
  source is selected.
- qmx_term.c: Radio menus over the network via the relay's terminal
  channel; USB behaviour unchanged.
- settings/config_io: relay_host / relay_port persisted and exported.
- webserver + web page: GET/POST /api/relay, radio_link in /api/status,
  Radio menu -> Radio source.

NAS application (tools/nas-relay):
- qmx_nas_relay.py: owns the QMX via libusb (no DSM kernel drivers),
  serves one Tab5 at a time; --probe and --fake bench modes.
- Dockerfile / docker-compose.yml for Synology Container Manager.

Docs: QMX-Panadapter-SharedViaNAS.pdf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
